#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:20
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Creates the repositories, drains the open PRs until the source settles, seeds them, re-points the declaration and verifies a fresh clone, then has the parent consume the result additively, makes the first release and checks every identifier dereferences. Nothing is seeded on an unknown readiness, and a fresh clone that could not run is not a pass. Called by kg-separation and sub-kg-lifecycle (bpmn-authoring: split by phase)."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:77
#. Diagram label
msgid "Drain: land, close or re-target the open PRs"
msgstr ""

