#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:36
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Runs the checks that decide the gateways: the tools' import closure and the content's lack of code, node identifiers against file paths, the standalone rehearsal, and dereferencing after release. A gate that cannot tell stops the process; it never reads as clean."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:81
#. Diagram label
msgid "Seed both repositories"
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:82
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Seed main, then bring the content and the tools in as reviewed pull requests with their history, so neither repository's first commit is unreviewable. The seed includes every publisher the declaration promises (`sub-kg-lifecycle` stage 10): a `qa` directory with `storage` needs `.github/workflows/publish-qa.yml`, the caller of the tools layer's `layer-qa-publish.yml`, and `test/results/` ignored. Without it the declared store is never written, and once the layer stops committing its results no reader finds them."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:150
#. Diagram label
msgid "settled"
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:124
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tag each repository, publish /v<major>/. From here the two are versioned independently; a tools release lists the content majors it supports."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:142
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The fresh clone could not be verified. Reported as could-not-check; the in-repo copy is not touched."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:59
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The owner creates the content and tools repositories and their Pages. Nothing is committed to them before this."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:116
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The parent pins the pair (a commit while staging, a version once released) — a code dependency as a `source.remote` instance in its root `index.config.json` (remote-mount skill), never a submodule — repoints its imports, and keeps its own copy until it is green with the dependency declared. Where `cat-harness.sdlc` is switched on, this step is the opt-in process `upstream-version-adoption` (`Process_UpstreamAdoption`, sdlc/processes/upstream-version-adoption.bpmn); it is not called from here, because a layer without that sub-graph does not have it (owner card Q-OPTIN-CALLS A, 2026-11-12)."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:26
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The person's decisions: whether to separate at all, authorising the extraction, creating the repositories, and the cutover that retires the parent's copy. An agent reports and waits at each; none of them may be relaxed by a package."
msgstr ""

#: processes/kg/kg-separation-move.bpmn:46
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The platform-side stages: the graph's identity (version, iriBase, nodeSchemas), moving harness output about it into the host, splitting the content from its tools, and making the parent consume the pair additively."
msgstr ""

